 "en-US-JennyNeural\u0000Three small words often go with the present perfect. ALREADY means 'before now', in positive sentences: “I've already changed the towels.” YET means 'up to now', in questions and negatives: “Have you cleaned the room yet?” “I haven't finished yet.” JUST means 'a very short time ago': “I've just brought your breakfast.”":{f:"b4610d5badf58349",d:20.904,v:0.710,a:0.200,b:20.040,wd:[0.24, 0.61, 1.08, 1.28, 1.68, 1.84, 2.2, 2.36, 2.94, 3.5, 3.99, 4.36, 4.85, 5.28, 5.44, 5.95, 6.63, 7.0, 7.4, 7.92, 8.23, 8.78, 9.02, 9.44, 9.64, 9.82, 10.19, 10.38, 11.08, 11.24, 11.88, 12.24, 12.6, 13.02, 13.36, 13.57, 13.94, 14.12, 14.62, 15.16, 15.48, 15.84, 16.21, 16.4, 16.8, 17.08, 17.38, 17.76, 18.08, 18.42, 18.92, 19.22],e:"000000SfkTQKRjonZIIXaXVLGE0MldL0QUQIQjePU0DQ00KiTLRNE00VP00PRKE00EE000000000000000000000000X-",w:"00----PZg---DFIIC55GKLJI---OSO--hWE6cQF8NX-LZ-cUy-mG4-wJH--PMINh--------0000000000000000---QNJBHNAheDDbhX7---G---NFLO9bnhaUKD94N----hc9Ws-QP--XrRL---beHG-R9v--RLFD--------cWKtLOIEIIwed---nmYEC---oW---XUKGGCB9---------00000-------------uWppZJ8WbA--VL---QCZhgbSHA63v---lRAx-HTx---PE8-YQ88guytZXPRMDU----------URtgL---ViXD-XE9FI98KfjdSW---------------00000000---dcv-ra-QQO--QZFZW----RWVONPc-------0000000000000000----hbo---8NQGg--QF8VRPHJM---OGJAs-+SVACJGLOKE969x----vcND--Z-----FOUbqWG4XFQUe---LJN----------00000000000000000",r:"--0000cSL000omjjpwwlhgij000dZd00KWnvPbmteU0gS0PX30Flx05ik00cfjeK00000000----------------000beiqkerKNooQKUu000l000emgdsQEKRXhosxe0000KPsV90bc00UAag000QNkl0as600agmo00000000PVh8gdjnjj5NO000EFTnp000DV000UXhllpqs000000000-----00000000000007WCCSitVQr00Wg000bpSKLQZkrvy6000Gar40kY4000cnt0TbttL738SUcafoX0000000000Xa8Lg000WJUo0UnsmjsthMIOZV000000000000000--------000OP60AR0bbd00bSmSV0000aWWdecP0000000----------------0000KQD000teblL00bmtWackif000dlir901ZWrpilgdhnsvs400006Peo00S00000mdXQBVlxUmbXN000gie0000000000-----------------"},
